#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119486 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc0992a-423e-5023-98d5-9d53c3b77788" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Curve"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "98c98a56-ca57-5dc6-9dc4-c40da53806f7" :question/math-academy-id "e-3063" :question/problem "Write down the integral that gives the arc length of the curve  $\\mathbf f (t) = \\langle 3 \\sin t, \\: 2\\sin 2t \\rangle$\nfrom $t =\\dfrac {3\\pi} 2$  to $t = 2\\pi.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/574a16e843a9c81e5fc9ddbbe2c0dc2c308ffcac4991bcbf48c7f45b4871c93b.png)" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf f'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡2t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119487 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e310cbe-9d6b-5bc4-960a-8813333bc8be" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Arc Length of a Planar Curve"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8932c22b-465f-5a48-962c-e53730e5ba40" :question/math-academy-id "e-3064" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf g (t) = \\langle 3 - 2 \\sin 2t, \\: 1 - 2\\cos 2t \\rangle$ from $t=\\dfrac \\pi 3$ to $\\pi.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/29c97e5963d451cc389944ef113764b2d15998448e773a02bb98c062207c2860.png)" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf g'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡2t+16{sin}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4t\\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =4(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119599 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1889ba1a-09d4-5021-9ed2-3e531f8d5ef0" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Arc Length of a Three-Dimensional Spatial Curve"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "118ad24e-627f-51ff-9b9c-9319c50956f9" :question/math-academy-id "e-6303" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/8573aedcd26cba038b2db072560cd3d6ba7676542888a2d9b8a356713eaf6724.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf r (t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\: \\cos t, \\: t \\rangle$\nfrom  $t =0$ to $t = 2\\pi.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\text{ }\\sqrt{2}\\,t{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(2\\pi -0) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330043 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc0992a-423e-5023-98d5-9d53c3b77788" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eda1903-6379-565f-99c0-d8768637792a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330045} {:answer/id #uuid "a5bbbab0-72dd-50cf-8c36-0102e6564c06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{2{e}^{t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330046} {:answer/id #uuid "283861f5-43ed-5426-be14-76882e7738b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{2{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330047} {:answer/id #uuid "da08c350-3fc6-51b3-9576-20e159e4d25d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330048} {:answer/id #uuid "c7003c81-e6bf-54ce-ba19-e4bea2c5efd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da08c350-3fc6-51b3-9576-20e159e4d25d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330048} :answer-field/id #uuid "712c7078-6f11-550c-9ba9-1fe27bfa93b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330044}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd39f385-6d0a-55b7-bb7b-d5fcb8c4110d" :question/math-academy-id "q-127427" :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$ from $t=-1$ to $t=1?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+({e}^{t})^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+{e}^{2t}+{cos}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1889ba1a-09d4-5021-9ed2-3e531f8d5ef0" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Arc Length of a Three-Dimensional Spatial Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a326f7cd-e00b-54c0-ab9f-590b9be9434f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117749} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb9c90d-0331-573b-b927-332415a3e3e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117750} {:answer/id #uuid "d44f81fe-365e-561c-a75f-c0401199df55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117751} {:answer/id #uuid "6f06dbb2-f486-597f-8823-cbcf836cf795" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117752} {:answer/id #uuid "7cc95fd8-7241-5de7-8389-734d1f51aa67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a326f7cd-e00b-54c0-ab9f-590b9be9434f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117749} :answer-field/id #uuid "78456853-af32-5f74-8527-d53770ea5c6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117748}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d7f25b66-94f4-5ecd-88ef-6b78d26ced87" :question/math-academy-id "q-33779" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom $t=1$ to $t=3.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\sqrt{3}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{3}t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3}t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)+3{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t>0$ for $t\\in [1,3].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={t}^{2}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =9-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc0992a-423e-5023-98d5-9d53c3b77788" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e290ec0-ed23-5528-bc18-4a7062dfb935" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int _{1}^{2}e^{t}\\sqrt{t^{2} + 2t + 4}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117785} {:answer/id #uuid "f058d6ff-6965-51d2-9b3f-a0cb15d51ea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int _{0}^{1}e^{t}(t + 2)dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117786} {:answer/id #uuid "ff8950e0-1b63-5027-b1bb-894cd121725f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int _{1}^{2}e^{t}\\sqrt{t^{2} + 2t + 5}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117787} {:answer/id #uuid "6e230b78-d713-59b8-ac85-31bb4b8aeede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int _{1}^{2}e^{t}\\sqrt{t^{2} + 2t + 6}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117788} {:answer/id #uuid "75a5a4de-3dd1-565b-80f0-e1edaf7b73f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int _{0}^{1}e^{t}\\sqrt{t^{2} + 2t + 2}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e230b78-d713-59b8-ac85-31bb4b8aeede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int _{1}^{2}e^{t}\\sqrt{t^{2} + 2t + 6}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117788} :answer-field/id #uuid "e58ff40c-133f-51e7-b56c-614aadcb292a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3bc45ddc-02bd-5a1e-bfa3-f99f90a0c552" :question/math-academy-id "q-33862" :question/problem "Which integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)={e}^{t}(\\,i+2\\,j+t\\,k)$ from  $t=1$ to $t=2?$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t{e}^{t})\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\,i+2{e}^{t}\\,j+(t{e}^{t}+{e}^{t})\\,k \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{({e}^{t})^{2}+(2{e}^{t})^{2}+({e}^{t}(t+1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+4{e}^{2t}+{e}^{2t}({t}^{2}+2t+1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}(1+4+{t}^{2}+2t+1)} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1889ba1a-09d4-5021-9ed2-3e531f8d5ef0" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Arc Length of a Three-Dimensional Spatial Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53517ea3-26c4-5902-be5e-7023b9c68892" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330066} {:answer/id #uuid "a43dd25b-f9c5-5b3c-bc3a-355433d5b591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330067} {:answer/id #uuid "0038e453-423d-585c-9ead-2b5ff1f2baf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330068} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b1533c-c1d2-5059-825f-ba540a3714d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330069} {:answer/id #uuid "1e072aa8-0925-56f3-ade4-e8a9dd23122e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53517ea3-26c4-5902-be5e-7023b9c68892" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330066} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5acc5f4-e4cb-5ddd-9fc2-1da017060484" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "23862600-8c37-5abe-8c3d-0dc47feee1b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-76906" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,4,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(2t)}^{2}+0+{(2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\,t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2\\sqrt{2}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1889ba1a-09d4-5021-9ed2-3e531f8d5ef0" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Arc Length of a Three-Dimensional Spatial Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "104f25b4-0991-5fa2-a86e-714183a38770" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330080} {:answer/id #uuid "137cc6ce-1302-55b8-93da-b31da784beb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330081} {:answer/id #uuid "612599a2-0d24-5584-8ec9-03156e2ea4e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330082} {:answer/id #uuid "d4f136fa-e4dd-52af-a412-280899af0845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330083} {:answer/id #uuid "f0e3a282-a6ab-5493-8dad-e6858e2cc307" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "137cc6ce-1302-55b8-93da-b31da784beb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330081} :answer-field/id #uuid "3670a8d8-8690-5738-a2b3-cb0bb5b0a50c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5bcd5987-bf48-5940-9557-fe98a5e45bbf" :question/math-academy-id "q-76914" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2},\\,2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,3t,\\,4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}+(3t)^{2}+{(4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡2t+9{t}^{2}+16{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}+9{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =5t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}5t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{5{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330085 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1889ba1a-09d4-5021-9ed2-3e531f8d5ef0" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Arc Length of a Three-Dimensional Spatial Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a22f314-d891-5169-9d3f-d4d1f4eb8a7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330087} {:answer/id #uuid "3b649431-c3be-51cd-9dc2-071bc864f0f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330088} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b4a854-0041-5a85-8731-a0328b89dee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330089} {:answer/id #uuid "e32967c6-13f5-5773-a742-212b2ba5fe59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330090} {:answer/id #uuid "73d98c4b-73b9-599d-9fa3-ead0e0a15b0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a22f314-d891-5169-9d3f-d4d1f4eb8a7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330087} :answer-field/id #uuid "b56fc8c5-8aac-5229-b630-e3cc573b124a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "69c5e2d0-9a19-5b71-8a53-1d2aae0ee046" :question/math-academy-id "q-77064" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨10,\\,\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(10),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,{t}^{2}-1,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+{(2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2}+1+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{({t}^{2}+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+t)|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =9+3-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e310cbe-9d6b-5bc4-960a-8813333bc8be" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Arc Length of a Planar Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ca0245b-3daf-552d-b91b-69163e39fa91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119206} {:answer/id #uuid "9a6dc5cd-bb20-56b4-b59a-9853a03f9d7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119207} {:answer/id #uuid "138a622c-b2f2-50fe-9ea1-ed8a76d566bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119208} {:answer/id #uuid "66832e5b-774c-5b1c-96dd-ba398909bf44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119209} {:answer/id #uuid "68466d2a-e907-5d07-bdcd-096ff96dbf1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "138a622c-b2f2-50fe-9ea1-ed8a76d566bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119208} :answer-field/id #uuid "10e1d94b-f6bc-5204-a2bb-cb30cf87ad9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0bd5879-0033-526b-bc0b-c6b5d407bf6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-77066" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1837/Source/Images/q-77066.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{g} ( t ) = \\langle  2 {t}^{3 / 2} , \\, 3 t \\rangle$ from $t = 0$ to $t = 3$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Differentiate: $\\mathbf g'(t)=\\langle3\\sqrt t,3\\rangle$, so the speed is $3\\sqrt{t+1}$. Therefore $$L=\\int_0^3 3\\sqrt{t+1}\\,dt=[2(t+1)^{3/2}]_0^3=2(8-1)=14.$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330106 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e310cbe-9d6b-5bc4-960a-8813333bc8be" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Arc Length of a Planar Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dc5d1c1-2837-56b3-a302-3c40a0d6d9f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330108} {:answer/id #uuid "315b78a7-a9f4-56a3-bbaa-a33dcb4a81ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330109} {:answer/id #uuid "b0dceaa5-1a7b-5113-bf8d-144eeb02d429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330110} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a975d7-d0c2-5d3f-a8db-b9dd175a8498" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330111} {:answer/id #uuid "fdcdaab1-718e-5f81-9526-2351f4961596" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdcdaab1-718e-5f81-9526-2351f4961596" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330112} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ddaa2dc-72c3-542f-b301-04ce5fa97c4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330107}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02904945-e53d-5a5a-8b80-5ae0efb5f8d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-77220" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/2efa774a3a7e97c23f695cfbdf681b53df055b8a84b84e2729af0a565841aeb7.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$\nfrom  $t=1$ to $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,,4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)}^{2}+{(4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t>0$ for $t\\in [1,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2(4-1) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
